=== REASONING ===
Goal: ship a production, native, parity version of BatteryDegradationForecastWidget
at the Allowed-Files path, then pass the gate (xcodebuild build+test on iOS and
macOS, swiftlint --strict, swiftformat --lint, check-placeholders).

Three independent, evidence-backed structural blockers make this impossible
WITHOUT editing files outside the single Allowed-Files path — which Rule 9
forbids and the prompt does NOT authorize (project.yml, Localizable.xcstrings,
and a new dashboard-host file are all out of scope):

  B1 — Build wiring. The prescribed output path
       `apps/apple/TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets/BatteryDegradationForecastWidget.*`
       is not a source root in `project.yml`, and the generated project proves a
       file there is compiled by NO target (and tested by NO test bundle). To
       include it, `project.yml` (sources: Sources/…) must be edited — OUT OF
       SCOPE. Therefore `xcodebuild -scheme TeslaSync … build test` and
       `-scheme TeslaSync-macOS … build test` cannot build or test this surface.
       Hard evidence (xcodegen generate from UNMODIFIED project.yml):
         grep -c 'BatteryDegradationForecast' TeslaSync.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj → 0
         grep -c 'dashboard-widgets'          TeslaSync.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj → 0

  B2 — Missing predecessor host. The prompt requires registering the surface in
       "the dashboard grid system" (draggable panel, registry id + size limits).
       No such host/registry exists in the Apple app (Rule 7: no predecessor
       bypass — do not invent one inside this single-file prompt; "Out of Scope"
       also excludes shared/atomic infrastructure).

  B3 — i18n catalog. Acceptance requires "Every i18n key from source has a
       matching key in P1/S10 catalog." The 10 `widget.forecast.*` / `widget.mo`
       keys are absent from Localizable.xcstrings; adding them edits a file
       outside Allowed-Files (Rule 9).

Rejected alternatives (and why):
  • Place the file under `Sources/…` so it compiles → violates Allowed-Files
